I’m looking for a forcing capture against Blue: with Green already eliminated and Blue at two losses, taking any Blue piece wins immediately. The key is to create a threat Blue cannot answer by moving just one piece.
I use the newly cleared (3,7) as the closing square of an edge trap. Red takes (0,7), threatening to play (3,6)–(3,7) next and sandwich both Blue pieces on the right edge; Blue must spend its turn breaking that line.

